   "text": "There are 396 calories in a serving of 32 grams of unsalted almonds because almonds are high in calories due to their fat content. These almonds are also rich in vitamins, minerals, and nutrients that support overall health. The calorie content is determined by the nutritional information of the almonds, which include a significant amount of healthy fats, proteins, and carbohydrates. ***\n\nAlmonds are a good source of essential vitamins such as vitamin E and B vitamins, as well as minerals like magnesium and potassium. They provide a range of nutrients that contribute to energy production and cellular function. The high nutrient density of almonds makes them a valuable addition to a balanced diet. ***\n\nThe calorie count of 396 per serving is based on the average nutritional content of a 32-gram serving of unsalted almonds. This includes the calories from fat, carbohydrates, and protein. Almonds are known for their ability to provide sustained energy due to their nutrient profile. ***\n\nConsuming almonds provides numerous health benefits, including improved heart health and better weight management. The vitamins, minerals, and nutrients in almonds support various bodily functions and contribute to overall well-being. Incorporating almonds into a diet can enhance nutritional intake and promote a healthier lifestyle.",
